Z||000000||johnt671||06-10-2001||01:57 PM||||problem somewhere causeing varing readings on the charge gage in the tach.  The charge always showed close to 15 amps but stared today to vary from a hair below 13 amps to almost 15 amps. the charge goes up and down for no reason.  It may be near 15 when I start out the for no reson drop to somewhere around 13.  Doesn't vary with engine speed or hiting bumps.  All connectons under the engine cover feel ok.  Alt. is around 2 years old and battery is 3 years old.  Car is an 84 4 cyl.  any ideas, please?||||reg||1
Z||000001||V8Fiero||06-10-2001||02:10 PM||||Had a similar problem with my V8. The guage would read around 15 when I first started the car and slowly drop after the car was running for so long. It turned out to be the Alternator. I suppose once it go hot in the engine compartment it really affected the alternator.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>84 SE V8 (FS or trade)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pffsig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
